### Describe the bug

During hydration, `element()` in `src/internal/client/dom/blocks/svelte-element.js` claims the existing SSR element (line 43–46) and then unconditionally calls `anchor.before(element)` (line 124), also for the node it just claimed. `before()` on a node that is already in the tree is a remove + insert. That:
- cancels and restarts every CSS animation/transition on the element and its subtree,
- fires childList mutations (removed + added) on the parent,
- disconnects/reconnects anything inside it (<iframe> reloads, <video> state, connectedCallback of custom elements).

A static element in the same position is not moved.

The visible symptom: any mount-time CSS animation inside a `<svelte:element>` plays once from first paint, then plays again from the start when hydration lands. On a cold load with hydration a second or two after first paint, that is a clearly visible "double flash". Warm loads hydrate before first paint, so it is easy to miss in development.

Verified in 5.55.2; the same unguarded `anchor.before(element)` is present in 5.57.1.

### Expected behaviour

During hydration a claimed `<svelte:element>` should stay where it is, like every other claimed node. `anchor.before(element)` is only needed when the element was created client-side (`create_element`) or the tag changed.

### Suggested fix (likely naive)

Track whether the element was claimed from the SSR DOM in this run and skip the re-insert in that case, e.g. in svelte-element.js:

```javascript
branches.ensure(next_tag, (anchor) => {
  if (next_tag) {
    var claimed = hydrating && element !== null; // element set from hydrate_node above
    element = claimed ? element : create_element(next_tag, ns);
    ...
    if (!claimed) anchor.before(element);
  }
  ...
});
```

(`hydrating` can be switched off at line 104 for void/empty elements before line 124 is reached, so the flag needs to be captured before `render_fn`.)

